# Codebase Audit, Security Hardening & Clean Code Refactoring Plan

This plan details the systematic audit, security remediation, and architecture refactoring for the Muslim Companion Android application following Google Engineering Practices and Android clean architecture standards.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Architecture & Security Improvements**:
> 1. **Dagger/Hilt Remote API Injection**: Migrate manual `Api.instance` companion object singletons (`PrayerApi`, `WeatherApi`, `QuranApi`, `GeminiApi`) into centralized Hilt `@Module` provision (`NetworkModule` / `AppModule`) with structured timeouts, shared `OkHttpClient`, and proper logging interceptor configuration.
> 2. **ProGuard / R8 & Moshi JSON Hardening**: Standardize all API response DTOs (`QuranApi.kt`) to Google Kotlin camelCase conventions with explicit `@Json(name = "...")` tags, preventing serialization failure during code shrinking.
> 3. **Eliminate Resource & Battery Leaks**:
>    - Fix `PrayerCountdownManager` infinite coroutine loop.
>    - Optimize `QiblaViewModel` sensor event processing by eliminating allocations in the 60Hz loop and guaranteeing unregistration in `onCleared()`.
>    - Fix uncancelled flow collection jobs in `AzkarViewModel.selectCategory()`.
> 4. **Resilience & Structured Error Handling**: Replace silent exception swallowing and `e.printStackTrace()` with structured `Log.e` tags and typed error states.

